          <formatted-text>
            <run fontsize='11'>Method and limits: sources are two Kaggle datasets (Bengaluru House Price Data; Housing Prices in Metropolitan Areas of India). 13,320 raw rows became 12,791 after de-duplication; 49 rows with implausible price/sqft (outside Rs 500-50,000) were excluded. Localities with fewer than 10 listings are not tiered. Medians are used throughout, and tiers are terciles of locality median price/sqft. City comparison uses a separate schema (Bengaluru 5,491, Hyderabad 1,997, Chennai 4,282 listings). Single snapshot with no listing dates; correlation is not causation.</run>
